# SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
sgi-replay 2
head sgi-mgras
# A host-to-screen DMA draw of a two-pixel row: a synthetic recording, not
# a driver trace (gr4 has no page on the DMA transaction; the staging is a
# reading of the engine). The two 'dma' lines preload what the transfer
# reads at plain node-0 addresses: the page-list entry (an 8-byte entry,
# frame 7) at 0x2018 and the eight source bytes at 0x7000.
#
# The command channel is entered as gl-pixels-rectwrite.replay does it
# (the 63 context words are that capture's): paint commands are ignored
# until a context has been selected.
#
# The block is staged IR_ALIAS, FILLMODE block type 5 (DMA write), XFRMODE
# 0x80 (32-bit alpha-first pixels), XFRSIZE, then the start and the
# executing end, so each source pixel reads alpha, blue, green, red and
# the first lands as 0x00112233. The DMA start word is 0xb1 (a word without
# bit 0 moves nothing), and the done token queued behind it raises the done
# flag the poll below waits for.
dma 0x2018 8 0000000000000007
dma 0x7000 8 0011223300445566
read 4 0x008000 0x0
write 4 0x011000 0x0
write 4 0x130500 0x000004fc
read 4 0x011020 0x00080000
write 4 0x011028 0x00080000
read 4 0x011020 0x0
write 4 0x120400 0x5420
write 4 0x120400 0xc000000
